==== Wireless LEDs ====

Wireless LEDs can be configured via NVRAM variables.

  * 0:ledbh9 -> Behaviour of 2.4GHz LED
  * 1:ledbh9 -> Behaviour of 5GHz LED
  * 0x7 makes the wireless LEDs on, when radios are enabled, and blink when there's activity
  * 0x88 makes the wireless LEDs off by default and blink when there's activity

Example:

   nvram set 0:ledbh9=0x7 && nvram commit

Restart the router for the changes to take effect.

---

The behaviour of both LEDs will be set at every boot. To disable the wireless LEDs, run these commands:

   nvram unset 0:ledbh9 unset 1:ledbh9 && nvram commit
   rm /etc/init.d/nvram

The first command unsets the variables for the wireless LEDs' behaviour.

The second command deletes the ''/etc/init.d/nvram'' file so the variables won't be set again.
